# Patches must reach the build byte for byte. Some upstream sources ship CRLF
# (xvidcore's src/nasm.inc is CRLF on all 213 lines), and a patch against one
# needs CRLF context to match. Git's end-of-line normalisation would rewrite
# that context to LF on checkout, and every hunk would then be rejected in
# %prep -- a failure that looks like a stale patch and is not one.
*.patch -text
*.diff -text
# Signing keys and signatures are data, never text to be normalised.
*.asc -text
*.sig -text
